  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P1] Unwrap cache metadata before JSON.parse in loadProfile",
      "body": "On every cache hit, `cached` is now an object of shape `{ value: string; stale: boolean }` rather than a JSON string, so `JSON.parse(cached)` stringifies it to `\"[object Object]\"` and throws a `SyntaxError` — breaking every cached profile load after the first. It is also a type error under the new `Cache.get` return signature (`JSON.parse` accepts `string`). The fix is to parse `cached.value` and handle `stale` as intended. Evidence: `src/cache.ts:5-7` (`get` now returns `readWithMetadata`'s metadata object) vs. the unchanged consumer at `src/profile.ts:18-19`.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/profile.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 19,
        "end": 19
      }
    }
